{"_v":1,"id":"matilda-the-musical-2013","cs":83,"rc":24,"bd":{"positive":22,"mixed":2,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":94,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/12/theater/reviews/matilda-the-musical-at-shubert-theater.html","d":"2013-04-11","q":"Rejoice, my theatergoing comrades."},{"cn":"David Rooney","o":"The Hollywood Reporter","s":93,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/review/matilda-theater-review-437819","d":"2013-04-11","q":"That song's soul-stirring mix of yearning and escape encapsulates what makes Matilda such a joy."},{"cn":"Gordon Cox","o":"Variety","s":93,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2013/legit/reviews/legit-review-matilda-1200348349/","d":"2013-04-11","q":"Matilda” turns out to be an explosion of joy, the most exhilarating and flat-out best musical since “Billy Elliot."},{"cn":"Jesse Green","o":"Vulture","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.vulture.com/2013/04/theater-review-matilda-the-musical.html","d":"2013-04-11","q":"Matilda the Musical is a triumph of imagination and craft, a show that manages to be both sweetly nostalgic and bracingly modern."},{"cn":"Chris Jones","o":"Chicago Tribune","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.chicagotribune.com/entertainment/theater/theaterloop/matilda-broadway-review,0,984726.column","d":"2013-04-11","q":"It was Dahl who invented Matilda, the spunky, over-achieving, proto-feminist, grrl-power heroine of what is far and away the best new musical of the Broadway season"},{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":86,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"http://www.washingtonpost.com/entertainment/theater_dance/matilda-on-broadway-its-magic-and-not-just-for-kids/2013/04/11/6a407c9a-a2ee-11e2-bd52-614156372695_story.html%20","d":"2013-04-12","q":"The show is a marvel of theatrical ingenuity, with Tim Minchin's lyrics crackling with wordplay and wit."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Associated Press","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://www.thenewstribune.com/2013/04/11/2553364/review-broadways-matilda-is-blast.html","d":"2013-04-11","q":"The English hit 'Matilda,' which opened Thursday at Shubert Theatre, is a witty musical adaptation of the beloved novel by Roald Dahl and is true to his bleak vision of childhood as a savage battleground."},{"cn":"Alexis Soloski","o":"The Guardian","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2015/aug/20/matilda-the-musical-review-still-a-revoltingly-subversive-success","d":"2013-04-12","q":"Matilda the Musical does feel uncomfortable at times, and it’s all the better for it."},{"cn":"Adam Feldman","o":"Time Out New York","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://www.timeout.com/newyork/theater/matilda?intcid=leader","d":"2013-04-11","q":"Matilda is wickedly smart and wildly fun; if your rotten mum or dad won't go, I suggest nicking their wallets and buying tickets yourself."},{"cn":"Terry Teachout","o":"The Wall Street Journal","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://online.wsj.com/article/SB10001424127887323741004578414582107592170.html","d":"2013-04-12","q":"It's smart, sweet, zany and stupendous fun."},{"cn":"Matt Wolf","o":"The Telegraph","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"http://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/theatre/theatre-reviews/9987399/Matilda-the-Musical-Shubert-Theatre-New-York-review.html","d":"2013-04-12","q":"But the tremendous heart and intelligence of the piece remains undimmed"},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Bloomberg","s":92,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/2013-04-11/five-star-matilda-brings-roald-dahl-to-broadway-review.html","d":"2013-04-11","q":"Welcome to the deliriously amusing, malevolent, heartwarming, head-spinning world of 'Matilda: The Musical.'"},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"NY1","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://brooklyn.ny1.com/content/ny1_living/theater_reviews/180296/ny1-theater-review---matilda-","q":"\"Matilda, The Musical\" is a conceptual triumph."},{"cn":"Matt Windman","o":"amNewYork","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://www.amny.com/urbanite-1.812039/theater-review-matilda-4-stars-1.5056914","q":"But it turned out to be an incredibly intelligent, heartfelt and entertaining work"},{"cn":"Elysa Gardner","o":"USA Today","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://www.usatoday.com/story/life/2013/04/11/broadway-review-matilda-the-musical/2063827/","d":"2013-04-11","q":"But Matilda is also affecting, and enchanting, in a way that homegrown hits of late haven't been."},{"cn":"Thom Geier","o":"Entertainment Weekly","s":85,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://www.ew.com/ew/article/0,,20364394_20690686,00.html","q":"You want to shout, ''Again!'' and demand that the cast start over from the very beginning so you might catch everything that you missed and revel in everything that you savored the first time around."},{"cn":"Robert Feldberg","o":"NorthJersey.com","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.northjersey.com/arts_entertainment/theater/202646671_Theater_review___Matilda___best_new_Broadway_musical_of_the_season.html?page=all","q":"With its pizazz, humor, style, intelligence and all-around entertainment quotient, \"Matilda\" is, far and away, the best new musical I’ve seen this season."},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Daily News","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://www.nydailynews.com/matilda-theater-review-article-1.1313830","d":"2013-04-11","q":"Matilda arrives on Broadway with a lot going for it, including an illustrious history as an award-winning hit in London."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Backstage","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.backstage.com/review/ny-theater/broadway/matilda-the-musical-royal-shakespeare-company-roald-dahl/","q":"It's built to dazzle, and it does."},{"cn":"Brendan Lemon","o":"Financial Times","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.ft.com/cms/s/2/2a8bf774-a298-11e2-9b70-00144feabdc0.html#axzz2QCUYitTz","d":"2013-04-11","q":"When you have such attributes you can afford to force audiences to lean forward a bit."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Newsday","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.newsday.com/entertainment/theater/matilda-the-musical-review-a-brit-hit-1.5047416","q":"Inventive and sinister pleasure, despite auditory problems"},{"cn":"Michael Feingold","o":"Village Voice","s":69,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://villagevoice.com/2013-04-10/theater/the-loud-new-musical-matilda-turns-dahl-into-dull/","d":"2013-04-10","q":"It's a terrible shame, it's an insult to the talented performers."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/matilda-the-musical-ig/","d":"2013-07-19","q":"Matilda is by far more rosy than tragic, and just as sweet as it is sentimental."},{"cn":"Michael Sommers","o":"New Jersey Newsroom","s":75,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"https://www.newjerseynewsroom.com/movies/matilda-broadway-review-a-british-bookworm-becomes-a-major-musical","q":"Regardless of my taste for the material, director Matthew Warchus’ production of the musical certainly is impressive."}],"au":{"score":82,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":82,"c":1009,"sr":4.1}}},"hi":"/images/shows/matilda-the-musical-2013/hero.webp","ta":"225 W 44th St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2013-03-04","ca":[{"n":"Bertie Carvel","r":"Miss Trunchbull"},{"n":"Gabriel Ebert","r":"Mr. Wormwood"},{"n":"Sophia Gennusa","r":"Matilda"},{"n":"Oona Laurence","r":"Matilda"},{"n":"Lesli Margherita","r":"Mrs. Wormwood"},{"n":"Bailey Ryon","r":"Matilda"},{"n":"Milly Shapiro","r":"Matilda"},{"n":"Lauren Ward","r":"Miss Honey"},{"n":"Frenie Acoba","r":"Lavender"},{"n":"Karen Aldridge","r":"Mrs. Phelps"},{"n":"Erica Simone Barnett","r":"Lavender"},{"n":"Judah Bellamy","r":"Tommy"},{"n":"Jack Broderick","r":"Bruce"},{"n":"Ava DeMary","r":"Alice"},{"n":"John Arthur Greene","r":"Doctor"},{"n":"Emma Howard","r":"Hortensia"},{"n":"Thayne Jasperson","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Tamika Sonja Lawrence","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Luke Kolbe Mannikus","r":"Bruce"},{"n":"Madilyn Jaz Morrow","r":"Alice"},{"n":"Sawyer Nunes","r":"Bruce"},{"n":"Jared Parker","r":"Nigel"},{"n":"John Sanders","r":"Sergei"},{"n":"Phillip Spaeth","r":"Rudolpho"},{"n":"Ryan Steele","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Betsy Struxness","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Samantha Sturm","r":"The Acrobat"},{"n":"Heather Tepe","r":"Lavender"},{"n":"Ben Thompson","r":"The Escapologist"},{"n":"Taylor Trensch","r":"Michael Wormwood"},{"n":"Beatrice Tulchin","r":"Amanda"},{"n":"Ted Wilson","r":"Eric"}]}